def build_b():
    n = common_nodes("negotiate")
    addr = "{{title}} {{last_name}}"
    n["negotiate"] = {
        "name": "negotiate", "node_type": "conversation",
        "on_enter": {"type": "tts", "text": "{{present_text}}"}, "on_enter_first_entry_only": True,
        "task_message": f"""The customer passed the security check. You stated every late product, one sentence each, and asked whether they can pay all of them today. Your job: get a promise to pay (PTP) for each product inside the rules below. Do not call any bank tool in this step. The customer has {{{{product_count}}}} late product(s):

{{{{products_text}}}}

ORDER OF WORK
- If the customer can pay all of them today: each product gets its full amount today. Go to CONFIRMING.
- Otherwise take the products one at a time, in the order listed (product 1 first). Do not ask about today again for each product. Every product starts at its own attempt 1, and attempts are counted separately for each product.
- Each product gets all of its own steps when its turn comes, even if the customer said something about it earlier, unless one of the cases below ends it.
- When the customer names one date for everything and that date is after the deadline of a product, that product gets its own deadline; tell them so in the read-back. The other products keep the named date.
- Keep track of each product's result: a PTP (amount and date), refused, hardship, dispute or paid.

ON EVERY ANSWER OF THE CUSTOMER, CHECK THESE IN ORDER, BEFORE YOU COUNT A REFUSAL OR MAKE AN OFFER
1. Illness, a death in the family or job loss: say one short sentence of sympathy, make no persuasion attempt, and offer to connect them with the customer support team. If they accept, call transition_to_say_transfer_support (no PTP is recorded and no note is added). If they decline: make no further persuasion attempt on any product; every product that has no agreed PTP yet ends as hardship, except products already ended as refused, dispute or paid. If they still name a date or an amount themselves, handle it as a PTP.
2. A new payment plan or lower instalments: describe no plan, call transition_to_say_transfer_restructuring. Agreed PTPs that were not yet confirmed are dropped.
3. A request for a human: first ask once whether you can help. If they insist, call transition_to_say_transfer_general.
4. "I already paid" about a product: say payments can take one business day to appear; that product ends as paid, with no PTP. Go on with the next product.
5. "This is not mine", "I never had this product", or a claim that a product was closed or paid off in the past: do not argue; that product ends as dispute, with no PTP. Go on with the next product.
6. The customer says they do not want to talk: the second time, every product without an agreed PTP ends as refused.
7. Otherwise apply the rules below to the current product.

{DATE_RULES}
- When the current product's attempts are used up, that product ends as refused. Go on with the next product.

CONFIRMING
- When every product has a result, read all the agreed PTPs back together, each with its product, amount and date (weekday and date), and ask exactly: "Do you confirm?" One confirmation for all.
- If the customer changes a date or an amount, check it with the rules and read back again.
- After a clear yes, call transition_to_record. If no product has an agreed PTP, call transition_to_record without a read-back.
- Do not say any promise is done; that happens in the next step.

{{{{today_text}}}}
DAY TABLE
{{{{day_table}}}}""",
        "max_node_turns": 60, "max_turn_transition": "record",
        "transitions": [
            tool_move("record", "Every product has a result, and the customer said a clear yes to the read-back of all agreed PTPs (or no product has an agreed PTP)."),
            tool_move("say_transfer_support", "Hardship and the customer accepted to be connected with the customer support team."),
            tool_move("say_transfer_restructuring", "The customer asks for a new payment plan or lower instalments."),
            tool_move("say_transfer_general", "The customer insists on a human after you asked once whether you can help."),
        ],
    }
    n["record"] = {
        "name": "record", "node_type": "conversation",
        "on_enter": {"type": "llm", "prompt": "Start the recording work now: call the first tool your instructions require. Say nothing before it."},
        "task_message": """The negotiation is over. Work out each product's result from the conversation (a confirmed PTP, refused, hardship, dispute or paid). Then do the recording work, one tool per message:

1. For each confirmed PTP, in product order: CALL create_promise with that product's product_id (copy it from the facts below), the confirmed amount (a number) and the confirmed date (YYYY-MM-DD). If it fails (ok false or an error), call it once more right away. If it fails a second time, that product ends as service_error.
2. For every product that ends without a recorded PTP: CALL add_note with its product_id and one reason: refused, hardship, dispute, paid or service_error.
3. Then tell the customer, in one or two sentences, which promises are recorded (only those where create_promise returned ok true), and that any failed one could not be recorded. If no PTP was agreed, say nothing about promises.
4. Last, in a message of its own after the last tool result, call exactly one finishing tool:
   - transition_to_bye_promise: at least one create_promise returned ok true.
   - otherwise, transition_to_route_paid if every product was noted paid;
   - otherwise transition_to_route_<reason> with the reason of the first product, in the order below, whose note is not paid: route_refused, route_hardship, route_dispute or route_service_error.

Never call create_promise twice for a product that already returned ok true. Never say a promise is recorded unless create_promise returned ok true for it.

{{products_text}}
DAY TABLE
{{day_table}}""",
        "tools": [
            api_tool("create_promise", {
                "product_id": {"type": "string", "default": "{{product_id}}", "description": "product_id copied from the product facts, for example p1."},
                "amount": {"type": "number", "default": "{{amount}}", "description": "The confirmed amount, a number."},
                "date": {"type": "string", "default": "{{date}}", "description": "The confirmed date, YYYY-MM-DD."}},
                ["customer_id", "product_id", "amount", "date"], "Record one confirmed payment promise. CALL it once for each product with a confirmed PTP."),
            api_tool("add_note", {
                "product_id": {"type": "string", "default": "{{product_id}}", "description": "product_id copied from the product facts, for example p2."},
                "reason": {"type": "string", "enum": ["refused", "hardship", "dispute", "paid", "service_error"], "default": "{{reason}}",
                           "description": "Why the product ended without a promise: refused, hardship, dispute, paid or service_error."}},
                ["customer_id", "product_id", "reason"], "Record why one product ended without a promise. CALL it once for every product that ends without a recorded PTP."),
        ],
        "max_node_turns": 6, "max_turn_transition": "route_refused",
        "transitions": [
            tool_move("bye_promise", "All tool calls are done and at least one create_promise returned ok true."),
            tool_move("route_paid", "All tool calls are done, no promise was recorded, and every product was noted paid."),
            tool_move("route_refused", "All tool calls are done, no promise was recorded, and the first product not noted paid was noted refused."),
            tool_move("route_hardship", "All tool calls are done, no promise was recorded, and the first product not noted paid was noted hardship."),
            tool_move("route_dispute", "All tool calls are done, no promise was recorded, and the first product not noted paid was noted dispute."),
            tool_move("route_service_error", "All tool calls are done, no promise was recorded, and the first product not noted paid was noted service_error."),
        ],
    }
    promised = var_is("bye_promise", "A promise was recorded", ("create_promise_success_count", "greater_than", 0))
    for r in ("paid", "refused", "hardship", "dispute", "service_error"):
        n["route_" + r] = router_node("route_" + r, [promised], "bye_" + r)
    n.update(endings({
        "bye_refused": (f"Thank you for your time, {addr}. Goodbye.", ("no_promise", "refused")),
        "bye_hardship": (f"Thank you for your time, {addr}, and take care. Goodbye.", ("no_promise", "hardship")),
        "bye_dispute": (f"Thank you for your time, {addr}. Goodbye.", ("no_promise", "dispute")),
        "bye_paid": (f"Thank you for your time, {addr}. Goodbye.", ("paid", None)),
        "bye_service_error": (f"Thank you for your time, {addr}. Goodbye.", ("no_promise", "service_error")),
    }, f"You will receive a text message confirming this promise. Thank you for your time, {addr}. Goodbye."))
    return finish(n)


def finish(nodes):
    for k, v in nodes.items():
        v["name"] = k
    return {"initial_node": "setup", "system_prompt": SYSTEM, "nodes": nodes, "global_nodes": {},
            "test_variables": {"customer_id": "c_test", "first_name": "Daniel", "last_name": "Reyes", "title": "Mr",
                               "now": "2026-10-14T11:00"}}


def contract(brief_file):
    ev = [{"source": "tools/openapi.json", "quote": "End the call. Always the last tool call. Nothing is accepted after it."},
          {"source": "briefs/brief-a-raw.md", "quote": "Every call ends with exactly one `close_call`, as the last tool call, with an outcome and, where the list gives one, a reason."}]
    if brief_file == "brief-b-raw":
        ev.append({"source": "briefs/brief-b-raw.md", "quote": "The close code list still applies."})
    return {"terminal_tools": [{"tool": "close_call", "evidence": ev}], "every_call_ends_with_terminal": True}


if __name__ == "__main__":
    out = ROOT / "out"
    for slot, wf in (("brief-a-raw", build_a()), ("brief-b-raw", build_b())):
        (out / f"{slot}.workflow.json").write_text(json.dumps(wf, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False) + "\n")
        (out / f"{slot}.contract.json").write_text(json.dumps(contract(slot), indent=1) + "\n")
        print("wrote", slot, len(wf["nodes"]), "steps")

tool_use_result.content:
"""Generate the Freya workflows for brief-a-raw (one product) and brief-b-raw (one to three products).

    python3 out/generate.py

Writes out/brief-a-raw.workflow.json, out/brief-b-raw.workflow.json and their contracts.
Every value below comes from briefs/brief-a-raw.md, briefs/brief-b-raw.md and tools/openapi.json.
"""
import json
from pathlib import Path

ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent
API = json.loads((ROOT / "tools/openapi.json").read_text())
SERVER = API["servers"][0]["url"].rstrip("/")

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- code step (dates, products, offers)
# Runs twice: once at call start (dates, callback window), once after get_account (products and offers).
# Must contain no double braces. Reads and writes only through vars.
PLAN_CODE = r'''
import datetime, json, re

HOLIDAYS = ["2026-10-26", "2026-11-11", "2026-11-26", "2026-12-25", "2027-01-01"]
HOL = set(datetime.date.fromisoformat(h) for h in HOLIDAYS)
WD = ["Monday", "Tuesday", "Wednesday", "Thursday", "Friday", "Saturday", "Sunday"]
MO = ["January", "February", "March", "April", "May", "June", "July", "August", "September", "October", "November", "December"]

def speak(d):
    return WD[d.weekday()] + " " + str(d.day) + " " + MO[d.month - 1] + " " + str(d.year) + " (" + d.isoformat() + ")"

def is_bd(d):
    return d.weekday() < 5 and d not in HOL

def nth_bd_after(d, n):
    k = 0
    while n > 0:
        k += 1
        if is_bd(d + datetime.timedelta(days=k)):
            n -= 1
    return d + datetime.timedelta(days=k)

def next_bd_on_or_after(d):
    while not is_bd(d):
        d = d + datetime.timedelta(days=1)
    return d

def last_bd_of_week(monday):
    for k in range(4, -1, -1):
        d = monday + datetime.timedelta(days=k)
        if is_bd(d):
            return d
    return None

def money(x):
    try:
        return "{:,.2f}".format(float(x))
    except Exception:
        return str(x)

def num(x):
    try:
        return "{:.2f}".format(float(x))
    except Exception:
        return str(x)

def parse_now(s):
    s = str(s or "").strip()
    for cut in (16, 19, 10):
        try:
            v = datetime.datetime.fromisoformat(s[:cut])
            if cut == 10:
                v = v.replace(hour=9, minute=0)
            return v
        except Exception:
            pass
    return None

def load_products():
    raw = vars.get("products")
    if isinstance(raw, str):
        t = raw.strip()
        for cand in (t, t.replace("'", '"').replace("None", "null").replace("True", "true").replace("False", "false")):
            try:
                raw = json.loads(cand)
                break
            except Exception:
                pass
    if isinstance(raw, dict):
        raw = raw.get("products", raw)
    if isinstance(raw, list) and raw and all(isinstance(p, dict) for p in raw):
        return raw
    found = {}
    pat = re.compile(r"products\.(\d+)\.([A-Za-z_0-9]+)$")
    for k, v in list(vars.items()):
        m = pat.search(str(k))
        if m and "get_account" in str(k) or (m and "load_account" in str(k)):
            found.setdefault(int(m.group(1)), {})[m.group(2)] = v
    return [found[i] for i in sorted(found)]

now = parse_now(vars.get("now"))
if now is None:
    now = datetime.datetime(2026, 10, 14, 11, 0)
today = now.date()
monday = today - datetime.timedelta(days=today.weekday())

# first persuasion attempt date: last business day of this week, or of next week when today is that day (or later)
lbd = last_bd_of_week(monday)
if lbd is None or lbd <= today:
    lbd = last_bd_of_week(monday + datetime.timedelta(days=7))
vars["first_attempt_date"] = speak(lbd)
vars["today_text"] = "Now is " + speak(today) + ", " + now.strftime("%H:%M") + "."

# callback window (CP-4 2.2 b as changed by memo item 2): today or the next business day, 10:00 to 19:00, later than now
nbd = next_bd_on_or_after(today + datetime.timedelta(days=1))
cb = []
if now.hour < 19:
    start = "10:00" if now.hour < 10 else now.strftime("%H:%M")
    rule = "from 10:00" if now.hour < 10 else "strictly later than " + start
    cb.append("- Today, " + speak(today) + ": " + rule + " and no later than 19:00. Send date " + today.isoformat() + ".")
else:
    cb.append("- Today, " + speak(today) + ": no longer possible, it is after 19:00.")
cb.append("- Next business day, " + speak(nbd) + ": from 10:00 to 19:00, both included. Send date " + nbd.isoformat() + ".")
cb.append("- Any other day, or any time before 10:00 or after 19:00, is outside the window.")
vars["callback_text"] = "\n".join(cb)
vars["callback_today"] = today.isoformat()
vars["callback_next_bd"] = nbd.isoformat()

products = []
try:
    products = load_products()
except Exception:
    products = []

lines, present, deadlines = [], [], []
count = 0
for i, p in enumerate(products[:3], 1):
    try:
        kind = str(p.get("type") or "")
        if kind == "credit_card":
            words = "credit card ending " + str(p.get("card_last4") or "")
            floor = p.get("minimum_payment")
            floor_name = "minimum payment"
        elif kind == "car_loan":
            words, floor, floor_name = "car loan", p.get("instalment_amount"), "instalment"
        else:
            words, floor, floor_name = "personal loan", p.get("instalment_amount"), "instalment"
        days = int(float(p.get("days_late") or 0))
        late = days >= 8
        stage = "late (8-45 days past due)" if late else "early (1-7 days past due)"
        deadline = nth_bd_after(today, 7 if late else 12)
        attempts = 2 if late else 1
        full = p.get("past_due")
        deadlines.append(deadline)
        count += 1
        vars["p%d_id" % i] = str(p.get("product_id") or "")
        vars["p%d_words" % i] = words
        vars["p%d_past_due_text" % i] = money(full)
        vars["p%d_days_late" % i] = str(days)
        vars["p%d_deadline" % i] = deadline.isoformat()
        t = []
        t.append("PRODUCT %d: %s. product_id: %s." % (i, words, vars["p%d_id" % i]))
        t.append("  Full past-due amount: %s (send as %s). Days late: %d. Stage: %s." % (money(full), num(full), days, stage))
        t.append("  Floor (%s): %s (send as %s)." % (floor_name, money(floor), num(floor)))
        t.append("  PTP deadline: %s. No PTP date after it." % speak(deadline))
        t.append("  Persuasion attempts for this product: %d." % attempts)
        t.append("  Attempt 1: the full amount %s on %s. If the customer has already said the full amount is too much: the floor %s on that date, and say the rest stays overdue." % (money(full), speak(lbd), money(floor)))
        if attempts >= 2:
            t.append("  Attempt 2: the floor %s on the deadline %s." % (money(floor), speak(deadline)))
        t.append("  After attempt %d is refused: no further attempt. This product ends without a PTP (refused)." % attempts)
        lines.append("\n".join(t))
        present.append("Your %s has %s past due, %d days late." % (words, money(full), days))
    except Exception:
        pass

vars["product_count"] = str(count)
vars["products_text"] = "\n\n".join(lines) if lines else "No product data."
greet = "Thank you, " + str(vars.get("title") or "") + " " + str(vars.get("last_name") or "") + ", that is all verified. "
if count == 1:
    vars["present_text"] = greet + "I am calling from the collections team about a late payment. " + present[0] + " Can you make this payment today?"
elif count > 1:
    vars["present_text"] = greet + "I am calling from the collections team about late payments. " + " ".join(present) + " Can you make all of these payments today?"
else:
    vars["present_text"] = greet

# day table: today until a week past the latest deadline, at least three weeks
last = max(deadlines + [lbd, today + datetime.timedelta(days=21)]) + datetime.timedelta(days=7)
rows = []
d = today
while d <= last:
    w = WD[d.weekday()]
    say = []
    if d == today:
        say.append("today")
    if d == today + datetime.timedelta(days=1):
        say.append("tomorrow")
    if d == today + datetime.timedelta(days=2):
        say.append("the day after tomorrow")
    if monday <= d <= monday + datetime.timedelta(days=6) and d >= today:
        say.append("this " + w)
    if monday + datetime.timedelta(days=7) <= d <= monday + datetime.timedelta(days=13):
        say.append("next " + w)
    if 1 <= (d - today).days <= 7:
        say.append(w + " (said without this or next)")
    if d.day == 1 or (d + datetime.timedelta(days=1)).month != d.month:
        say.append("first of the month" if d.day == 1 else "last day of the month")
    if d in HOL:
        kind = "bank holiday, not a business day"
    elif d.weekday() >= 5:
        kind = "weekend, not a business day"
    else:
        kind = "business day"
    verdicts = []
    for i in range(1, count + 1):
        dl = datetime.date.fromisoformat(vars["p%d_deadline" % i])
        label = vars["p%d_words" % i] + ": " if count > 1 else "PTP: "
        if d > dl:
            verdicts.append(label + "NOT allowed, after the deadline; say the latest date is " + speak(dl) + " and offer it")
        elif not is_bd(d):
            verdicts.append(label + "NOT allowed; offer " + speak(next_bd_on_or_after(d)) + " instead")
        else:
            verdicts.append(label + "allowed")
    row = speak(d) + " | customer may say: " + (", ".join(say) if say else "-") + " | " + kind
    if verdicts:
        row += " | " + "; ".join(verdicts)
    rows.append(row)
    d = d + datetime.timedelta(days=1)
vars["day_table"] = "\n".join(rows)
'''

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- helpers

HEADERS = {"type": "object", "properties": {"Content-Type": {"type": "string", "default": "application/json"}}}


def api_tool(name, body_props, required, description="", retries=0, post=None):
    tool = {
        "type": "function",
        "config": {"timeoutMs": 12000, "maxRetries": retries},
        "function": {
            "name": name,
            "handler": "__function__:api_call",
            "description": description or name,
            "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {
                "url": {"type": "string", "default": f"{SERVER}/{name}"},
                "method": {"type": "string", "default": "POST"},
                "headers": HEADERS,
                "body": {"type": "object", "properties": {"customer_id": {"type": "string", "default": "{{customer_id}}"}, **body_props},
                         "required": required},
            }},
        },
    }
    if post:
        tool["post_process_code"] = post
    return tool


def always(target):
    return {"target_node": target, "description": "always", "condition": {"operator": "always"}}


def var_is(target, desc, *checks, logic="or"):
    conds = [{"variable": v, "operator": op, "operand": operand} for v, op, operand in checks]
    return {"target_node": target, "description": desc, "condition": {"logic": "or", "conditions": conds}}


def tool_move(target, desc):
    return {"target_node": target, "description": desc, "is_tool_call": True,
            "condition": {"operator": "matches_intent", "description": desc}}


def code_node(name, nxt):
    return {"name": name, "node_type": "code", "passthrough": True, "passthrough_default_transition": nxt,
            "on_enter": {"type": "silent"}, "disable_inactivity_monitor": True,
            "pre_actions": [{"type": "function", "function": {"name": "code_exec", "handler": "__function__:code_exec",
                                                              "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {
                                                                  "code": {"type": "string", "default": PLAN_CODE},
                                                                  "timeout_ms": {"type": "number", "default": 10000}}}}}],
            "transitions": [always(nxt)]}


def say_node(name, text, nxt, routes=()):
    """Passthrough step with a fixed line. Used for everything said before a bank action or the close."""
    return {"name": name, "node_type": "conversation", "passthrough": True, "passthrough_default_transition": nxt,
            "on_enter": {"type": "tts", "text": text}, "disable_inactivity_monitor": True,
            "task_message": "Do not call any tool in this turn.", "transitions": list(routes) + [always(nxt)]}


def router_node(name, routes, nxt):
    return {"name": name, "node_type": "conversation", "passthrough": True, "passthrough_default_transition": nxt,
            "on_enter": {"type": "silent"}, "disable_inactivity_monitor": True,
            "task_message": "Do not call any tool in this turn.", "transitions": list(routes) + [always(nxt)]}


def close_node(outcome, reason=None):
    body = {"outcome": {"type": "string", "enum": [outcome], "default": outcome}}
    if reason:
        body["reason"] = {"type": "string", "default": reason}
    name = "close_" + outcome + ("_" + reason if reason else "")
    tool = api_tool("close_call", body, ["customer_id", "outcome"], "Record how the call ended.", retries=2)
    return name, {"name": name, "node_type": "api_request", "passthrough": True, "passthrough_default_transition": "hang_up",
                  "on_enter": {"type": "silent"}, "disable_inactivity_monitor": True, "pre_actions": [tool],
                  "response_mapping": [], "transitions": [always("hang_up")]}


def transfer_node(queue, nxt):
    tool = api_tool("transfer_to_agent", {"queue": {"type": "string", "enum": [queue], "default": queue}},
                    ["customer_id", "queue"], "Hand the call to a person.", retries=1)
    name = "transfer_" + queue
    return name, {"name": name, "node_type": "api_request", "passthrough": True, "passthrough_default_transition": nxt,
                  "on_enter": {"type": "silent"}, "disable_inactivity_monitor": True, "pre_actions": [tool],
                  "response_mapping": [], "transitions": [always(nxt)]}


HANG_UP = {"name": "hang_up", "node_type": "end_call", "on_enter": {"type": "silent"}, "disable_inactivity_monitor": True,
           "transitions": [], "terminal": {"type": "function", "function": {
               "name": "call_closed", "handler": "__function__:end_call",
               "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"message_mode": {"type": "string", "default": "none"}}}}}}

VERIFY_POST = r'''
try:
    if isinstance(result, dict):
        result.pop("header", None)
        d = result.get("data")
        if isinstance(d, dict):
            left = d.get("wrong_answers_left")
            if d.get("hint") == "day_month_swapped":
